      "content": "The most equitable distribution method is a lottery system because it ensures fairness by giving every applicant an equal chance regardless of their background or location. Relying on income levels or transit proximity creates a two-tiered system that privileges the already advantaged while leaving the most vulnerable without a voice. We must stand behind a transparent lottery to uphold the core principle that housing rights should not be determined by who you know or where you live.",
