      "content": "That seems a bit dismissive of the transit argument though. If we don't prioritize transit proximity, we're basically just moving people into isolated pockets where they can't get to work or school without a car, which just keeps them stuck. Doesn't focusing on transit access actually provide more long-term equity than just a random draw?",
